# No redirect rules — deliberately. This file exists to record why, because the
# obvious thing to put here does not work.
#
# The demo at /demo is a client-side-routed SPA (react-router), so a deep link
# like /demo/note/quarterly-review has no file behind it and needs a fallback.
# The standard Cloudflare Pages recipe is:
#
#     /demo/*  /demo/index.html  200
#
# Pages REJECTS that rule: "Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been
# ignored", because it normalises the destination /demo/index.html back to
# /demo/, which matches /demo/* again. Wrangler reports "Parsed 0 valid redirect
# rules" and deep links silently 404. Any splat pointing at an index.html is
# refused the same way.
#
# Listing each route explicitly (with :placeholder segments for /note/:id) does
# parse — all 14 rules accepted — but it still does not work: Pages resolves them
# as real 3xx redirects to /demo/ rather than 200 rewrites, so the path is thrown
# away and the visitor lands on the note grid instead of their note. Worse, the
# redirect is cacheable, so a browser that saw it once keeps doing it.
#
# What actually works: Cloudflare Pages serves the nearest parent 404.html for an
# unmatched path, with the URL left intact. So the demo build writes a copy of
# its own shell to /demo/404.html and that IS the SPA fallback — no rules, no
# loops, no redirects, clean URLs, and one origin shared with the site (which is
# how a visitor's light/dark choice follows them into the demo and back).
#
# See the `demoBuild()` plugin in papyra.web/vite.config.ts.
#
# If you ever do add a rule here, check it took effect with:
#     pnpm --filter papyra-app run preview:cf
# which prints how many rules actually parsed.
